# tar.bgn / TarFile: one 512-byte ustar header followed by its payload.
# oct2int() walks the size field comparing each byte against the character
# literals '0' and '7', so every one of the 12 bytes must be an octal digit
# (a NUL-terminated size, as real tar writers emit, would fail the assert).
68 65 6c 6c 6f 2e 74 78 74 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 # name [100]u8
30 30 30 30 36 34 34 00 # mode [8]u8
30 30 30 30 30 30 30 00 # uid [8]u8
30 30 30 30 30 30 30 00 # gid [8]u8
30 30 30 30 30 30 30 30 30 30 31 32 # size [12]u8 = "000000000012" octal = 10
30 30 30 30 30 30 30 30 30 30 30 00 # mtime [12]u8
20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 # chksum [8]u8
30 # type :u8
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 # linkname [100]u8
75 73 74 61 72 00 # magic :"ustar\0"
30 30 # version [2]u8
72 6f 6f 74 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 # uname [32]u8
72 6f 6f 74 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 # gname [32]u8
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 # devmajor [8]u8
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 # devminor [8]u8
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 # prefix [155]u8
00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 # padding [12]u8
48 65 6c 6c 6f 20 74 61 72 0a # data [len]u8 = "Hello tar\n"
